></span><a href=\"/w/images/e/ea/Weight_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> Weight: 0.5 kg (1 lb)</li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/2/26/Gold_Icon.png/25px-Gold_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/2/26/Gold_Icon.png 1.5x\"><img alt=\"Price: 14 gp\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/2/26/Gold_Icon.png/25px-Gold_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/2/26/Gold_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> Price:  14  gp</li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/3/3c/Ico_stats.png/25px-Ico_stats.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/3/3c/Ico_stats.png/38px-Ico_stats.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/3/3c/Ico_stats.png 2x\"><img alt=\"￼START_WIDGET&quot;'-e58e7abed45d5939END_WIDGET ￼START_WIDGET&quot;'-4d64ddc4a2c64841END_WIDGET\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/3/3c/Ico_stats.png/25px-Ico_stats.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/3/3c/Ico_stats.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <details class=\"bg3wiki-uid\">\n<summary>UID</summary>\n<code class=\"bg3wiki-uid-box\">S_UND_ClericResearch</code>\n</details> <span class=\"bg3wiki-uid-link\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://bg3.norbyte.dev/search?q=name:S_UND_ClericResearch\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img alt=\"https://bg3.norbyte.dev/search?q=name:S_UND_ClericResearch\" src=\"/w/images/7/70/Search_icon.svg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></a></span></span> <details class=\"bg3wiki-uid\">\n<summary>UUID</summary>\n<code class=\"bg3wiki-uid-box\">606542f8-af80-4102-b849-84e73d8a7f12</code>\n</details> <span class=\"bg3wiki-uid-link\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://bg3.norbyte.dev/search?q=uuid:606542f8-af80-4102-b849-84e73d8a7f12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img alt=\"https://bg3.norbyte.dev/search?q=uuid:606542f8-af80-4102-b849-84e73d8a7f12\" src=\"/w/images/7/70/Search_icon.svg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></a></span></span></li></ul>\n</div>   \n<div style=\"clear: both;\"></div></div>\n    <h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Where_to_find\"> Where to find </span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-tooltip-box\">\n<ul><li>Near the entrance to the backyard of <a href=\"/wiki/Arcane_Tower\" title=\"Arcane Tower\">Arcane Tower</a> <span class=\"bg3wiki-coordinates\">X:&nbsp;-27&nbsp;Y:&nbsp;-292</span></li></ul>\n</div>  <h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Text\"> Text </span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-book-text\">\n<p>THE ANTIMAGIC PROPERTIES OF SUSSUR TREE FLOWERS\n</p><p>By L. De Hurst\n</p><p><br>\nFor those knowing about <a href=\"/wiki/Sussur_Tree_Bark\" title=\"Sussur Tree Bark\">sussur trees</a>, their magical properties have always been a topic of debate; not only their ability to create an antimagic aura, which is complete enough that even those unattuned to the <a href=\"/wiki/Weave\" title=\"Weave\">Weave</a> can feel its effect, but also - and most interestingly to those living in the World Above - the ways its roots, bark, and flowers can be harnessed to make magic items. Rumours of such items are rare, but spread in settlements bordering the <a href=\"/wiki/Underdark\" title=\"Underdark\">Underdark</a>. Their existence, however, has never been confirmed by any of our <a href=\"/wiki/Cleric\" title=\"Cleric\">clerics</a>, nor by any other reputable scholars. I hypothesised that these items are no mere legends, and indeed, in this treatise I will endeavour to explain how I myself created items that have antimagic properties, and that use the magical absorption of <a href=\"/wiki/Sussur_Bloom\" title=\"Sussur Bloom\">sussur tree flowers</a> as a power source.\n</p><p><br>\n[Lines have been drawn on the following pages, as if the author intended to fill them with writing, but the remainder of the thin book is blank.]\n</p>\n</div>    \n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260714195121\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1, no‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.055 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1608/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 34324/4194304 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 11021/4194304 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 29/200\nExpensive parser function count: 2/750\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 0/1000\nLua time usage: 0.011/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 931921/52428800 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   44.554      1 Template:MiscItemPage\n100.00%   44.554      1 -total\n 56.67%   25.250      7 Template:Icon_text\n 50.83%   22.647     17 Template:Trim\n 23.29%   10.378      2 Template:Uid\n 15.13%    6.741      1 Template:Main_only\n 13.20%    5.883      2 Template:Icon_link\n 13.13%    5.852      2 Template:Template_style\n 10.37%    4.622      1 Template:Ifexist\n 10.34%    4.607      1 Template:Books\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key bg3wiki:pcache:idhash:12801-0!canonical and timestamp 20260714195121 and revision id 391082. Rendering was triggered because: unknown\n -->\n</div>"}